{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>A different spirit with him.</b> Different from the spies, for the righteous is 'other' than the wicked. And so you find in the case of Seth (Genesis 4:25): ״כי שת לי אלהים זרע אחר״ — 'for Elohim has appointed me another seed' — because Seth the righteous, who was in place of Abel, was 'other' than Cain the wicked, for good is other than evil and likewise evil is other than good. And this is the sense of (Exodus 20:3) ״אלהים אחרים״ — 'other Elohim' — and (ibid. 34) ״לא תשתחוה לאל אחר״ — 'you shall not bow down to another El.' If so, the word אחר when mentioned in connection with evil denotes good, and when mentioned in connection with good denotes evil." "<b>And I will bring him into the land etc.</b> Here too HaShem alluded to the designated name backward (למפרע), to indicate that the attribute of judgment was stretched out against them, and therefore He decreed upon them that they would sink in the wilderness and go backward (למפרע) and retrace their steps toward the Sea of Reeds. From this Moses said to them when they wanted to go ahead and go up the mountain: ״למה זה אתם עוברים את פי ה' והיא לא תצלח״ — 'Why are you transgressing the word of HaShem when it will not succeed' — and therefore He said to them, ״כי על כן שבתם מאחרי ה'״ — 'because you have turned back from following HaShem' — and from this you are condemned to turn backward, ״ולא יהיה שמי הגדול עמכם״. And the sense of יושב בעמק: lying in wait for you."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {1 "The Hebrew lemma includes a truncated citation sequence spanning Numbers 14:24–25, including words from the end of v. 24 through v. 25 (והעמלק'י, יושב בעמק); rendered as a composite lemma head reflecting the full span he quotes. Final quotation ולא יהיה שמי הגדול עמכם is from Exodus 33:2–3 paraphrased; left without verse citation as he gives none."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], 